WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:05.960
We could end the pandemic as a pandemic by
the Fourth of July if we took action right

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:06.960
now.

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:08.830
Wouldn't mean we have no new cases, certainly.

00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:12.150
But we could end the pandemic phase.

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:13.349
I guess we would call it.

00:00:13.349 --> 00:00:17.880
And I know that many of you know, we've already
missed a number of opportunities to do this.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:22.560
Back on March 5th, I'm being very generous
by looking at March 5th.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:25.870
We had all the information we needed about
the spread of the virus.

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:27.680
We should have taken immediate action.

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:33.969
Donald Trump should have said to all 50 governors,
listen, we need a 50 state stay at home order.

00:00:33.969 --> 00:00:38.719
We have some very, very difficult days ahead.

00:00:38.719 --> 00:00:43.749
But we will be better off if we all do this
now instead on March 5th.

00:00:43.749 --> 00:00:45.210
We did nothing on March 5th.

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:48.799
We ended up doing only five hundred or so
tests by March 15th.

00:00:48.799 --> 00:00:51.750
We were still only doing about a thousand
tests a day.

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:57.089
By March 25th, we were finally up to 80000
tests, which was still not nearly enough.

00:00:57.089 --> 00:00:58.569
We were so behind.

00:00:58.569 --> 00:01:04.750
And still to this day we aren't doing enough
tests and we don't have any federal contact

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:05.750
tracing initiative.

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:08.369
So opportunities have come and gone.

00:01:08.369 --> 00:01:13.229
But once again, we have an opportunity in
front of us to deal with what we are dealing

00:01:13.229 --> 00:01:18.100
with right now and we could be in very good
shape nationally by July 4th.

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:24.060
Alex Tabarrok and Pooja All Hiver wrote a
really good piece in The Washington Post outlining

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:29.030
the bipartisan, bipartisan plan that they
participated in putting together.

00:01:29.030 --> 00:01:33.570
And it's important that this plan considers
the medical and the economic.

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:36.430
I've been taking the economic seriously from
day one.

00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:42.150
The right has been having a grand old time
framing leftists as not caring about the economy,

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:46.270
as not caring about unemployment, not caring
about economic destruction.

00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:50.791
The truth is, I and most serious leftists
have been concerned from day one with the

00:01:50.791 --> 00:01:51.791
economy.

00:01:51.791 --> 00:01:56.549
And the reality is that six months of rolling
dock lockdowns in some parts of the country,

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:58.619
some open, close, open, close.

00:01:58.619 --> 00:02:01.110
That's not going to be good for the economy
either.

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:05.920
There's a plan that's been written and the
test the testing element is a big part of

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:06.920
that plan.

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:09.060
We need to dramatically increase testing.

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:10.299
How innovative.

00:02:10.299 --> 00:02:14.069
It's not it's not surprising, but we are still
not testing enough.

00:02:14.069 --> 00:02:18.349
But the test levels are very specifically
outlined by this plan.

00:02:18.349 --> 00:02:25.500
We need to be testing everyone who has symptoms
and all of their contact contacts and have

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:28.400
enough capacity for what we call surveillance
testing.

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:34.060
People just go in even without symptoms because
there is such such asymptomatic spread.

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:39.510
We need everyone who has the disease and their
contacts to self isolate.

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:44.439
We may need hotel rooms for people to be able
to self isolate depending on their situation

00:02:44.439 --> 00:02:45.439
at home.

00:02:45.439 --> 00:02:50.349
We may need stipends for people who are self
isolating while they cannot work.

00:02:50.349 --> 00:02:55.030
And what the plan does that is really important
is it divides the country into three types

00:02:55.030 --> 00:02:59.180
of zones green zones, yellow zones and red
zones.

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:04.439
And the plan acknowledges, which a lot of
right wingers want, that rural Montana doesn't

00:03:04.439 --> 00:03:07.810
have to do the same thing that New York City
needs to do.

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:13.480
Green Zone would mean fewer than one in 36000
are infected.

00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:15.709
You can do large gatherings in green zones.

00:03:15.709 --> 00:03:22.000
You don't need a mask in green zones unless
you are part of or around folks who are in

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:23.950
vulnerable populations.

00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:31.180
You need one test per day for every 10000
people in green zones and five contact tracers

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:33.290
for every hundred thousand people.

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:35.140
That is not a lot for the green zones.

00:03:35.140 --> 00:03:38.849
Now, right now, there are not very many green
zones.

00:03:38.849 --> 00:03:43.100
Two weeks ago, we could have had 19 million
Americans in green zones based on our testing

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:44.100
levels.

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:48.180
Right now, we don't have any active green
zones that are meeting these requirements.

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:49.579
Then we get the yellow zones.

00:03:49.579 --> 00:03:53.129
Yellow zones are for most of the country right
now.

00:03:53.129 --> 00:03:57.450
Two hundred and ninety eight million Americans
right now would be in what we call yellow

00:03:57.450 --> 00:03:58.900
zones.

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:05.930
That's where the disease prevalence is, somewhere
between point 0 0 2 percent and 1 percent.

00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:07.750
OK, in the yellow zones.

00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:10.530
The economy can reopen.

00:04:10.530 --> 00:04:12.430
Mandatory masks for everyone.

00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:17.630
And you need twenty five hundred tests, tests
for each daily death.

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:20.320
Plus much more contact tracing.

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:25.380
You need to have enough contact tracing to
contact every person who's been in touch with

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:28.260
an infected individual within 12 hours.

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:29.500
Why within 12 hours?

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:31.640
Because if you wait three days, it's too late.

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:34.510
And those people have been going around potentially
spreading the disease.

00:04:34.510 --> 00:04:41.080
So, for example, based on the last few days
of deaths, New Jersey would need 250000 tests

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:42.340
per day.

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:46.330
But Maryland would only need eighty seven
thousand tests per day.

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:49.010
These are much bigger numbers than what we
have.

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:54.440
But these are not cartoonishly high numbers
based on on the models that we've seen.

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:57.860
So you've got your green zones and your yellow
zones, then you've got your red zones.

00:04:57.860 --> 00:05:01.450
Red zones are more than 1 percent of the population
is infected.

00:05:01.450 --> 00:05:05.410
Right now, there are about 30 million people
in that situation.

00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:08.320
That's just under 10 percent of the country.

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:13.830
So in those red zones, you have everything
that the yellow zones have in terms of testing

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:15.000
and tracing.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:18.580
But you also have a stay at home order if
you follow it.

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:23.981
The red zone becomes yellow relatively quickly
by four weeks and most analysis and then you

00:05:23.981 --> 00:05:29.000
move to yellow and then the whole country
could be at minimum at yellow.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:33.000
By the Fourth of July, that means the whole
country could be open, although yellow zones

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:37.510
would still have more precautions like mandatory
masks and we could be at green by the end

00:05:37.510 --> 00:05:38.700
of the summer.

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:40.260
We're not even close on testing.

00:05:40.260 --> 00:05:44.280
We're now testing about three hundred and
fifty thousand three seventy five thousand

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:45.280
a day.

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:49.680
We need somewhere between three and five million
a day.

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:53.060
And based on current numbers, we're nowhere
near that.

00:05:53.060 --> 00:05:56.110
This can be done, but we're way behind.

00:05:56.110 --> 00:05:59.410
If we started today, we could be in mood.

00:05:59.410 --> 00:06:04.160
Pretty good shape for moving red zones to
yellow and yellow to green heavily around

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:05.490
the Fourth of July.

00:06:05.490 --> 00:06:10.280
Seems to be no political desire at the federal
government trumps acting like we won.

00:06:10.280 --> 00:06:12.460
He's talking about superduper missiles.

00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:13.730
But this is a plan that works.

00:06:13.730 --> 00:06:15.550
Test, trace and isolate North Korea.

00:06:15.550 --> 00:06:19.370
I'm sorry South Korea succeeded with it at
the earliest.

00:06:19.370 --> 00:06:20.870
New Zealand did it.

00:06:20.870 --> 00:06:22.650
Taiwan did it.

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:26.630
Greece had a milder version and they still
did it, although it took a little bit longer.

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:30.270
Greece's is looking at opening up for travel
very, very soon.

00:06:30.270 --> 00:06:33.120
Prevention is cheaper than the cure.

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:37.260
Testing is cheaper than both the economic
destruction and the costs of treating way

00:06:37.260 --> 00:06:38.730
more sick people.

00:06:38.730 --> 00:06:40.040
Here's another plan.

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:41.790
The plan is based on right now.

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:42.790
It's mid-May.

00:06:42.790 --> 00:06:43.790
We could do this.

00:06:43.790 --> 00:06:43.800
We could be in very good shape by July 4th.

